                                "sense_id": "875a62bc-3feb-3368-a77c-ff276a1efb29",
                                "text": "They shall provide all bottlers with face guards,[…]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b2b85870-dcbd-4bb4-bfb7-de6464d92b7a",
                                "sense_id": "875a62bc-3feb-3368-a77c-ff276a1efb29",
                                "text": "1994 May 30, Shawn Willett, PC tools help Coke add life to flat AS/400 data, InfoWorld, page 63,\nSuch data is of great value both to the bottlers and to Coca-Cola′s sales and marketing groups.\n“When the bottler looks at this information, he might be interested in how a certain supermarket is performing, while we in the company are interested in how much, for example, McDonald’s is buying in the Southeast,” Aviles notes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "186c8279-bd7f-42f7-9d4b-f53851cc9442",
                                "sense_id": "875a62bc-3feb-3368-a77c-ff276a1efb29",
                                "text": "Note 8, “Noncontrolled Bottling Affiliates” (Appendix A), indicates that PepsiCo owns approximately 40 percent of the common stock of some of its bottlers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cd7ffd30-7a0f-4d0b-8f58-074f75937b83",
                                "sense_id": "875a62bc-3feb-3368-a77c-ff276a1efb29",
                                "text": "Maritime Transport runs a train from the bottler of Cola-Cola in Tilbury, six days a week. It started in 2022, and the bottler says it will save four million road miles a year and 15,000 lorry journeys, moving 2.5 million cans and bottles on the train each day."
                            }
                        ]
